From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thororen <78185467+thororen1234@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:55:17 -0400
Subject: fix: restore Windows 7 sandbox support

Restore what Chromium did before dropping Windows 7 (M109), adapted to
the current sandbox:

* Windows 7 only supports the DEP and SEHOP process creation
  mitigations, passed as a DWORD on 32-bit, and has no
  Get/SetProcessMitigationPolicy, so restore the version checks.
* PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_JOB_LIST requires Windows 10, so assign the
  suspended target to its job after creation, breaking away from any job
  the broker is in on Windows 7 (no nested jobs), or staying in it when
  breaking away isn't allowed.
* ProcessHandleTable requires Windows 8.1, so the handle closer probes
  handle values instead before that.
* Skip AppContainers and the DeviceApi handle before Windows 8.
* Only renderers and the GPU process are sandboxed on Windows 7; other
  child processes rely on Windows 10 sandbox features, so they run
  unsandboxed and are told so with --no-sandbox.

This patch is needed for Windows 7 support and is not suitable for
upstreaming.

